						<div class="elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default">
					<div class="has_eae_slider elementor-column elementor-col-50 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-064511f" data-eae-slider="99585" data-id="064511f" data-element_type="column">
			<div class="elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated">
						<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-cdc32f6 eael-infobox-shape-square eael-infobox-hover-img-shape-square elementor-widget elementor-widget-eael-info-box" data-id="cdc32f6" data-element_type="widget" data-widget_type="eael-info-box.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					        <div class="eael-infobox icon-on-left">
	            <div class="infobox-icon">

                            <img class="lazy" decoding="async" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%20275%20183'%3E%3C/svg%3E" data-src="https://5mglobal.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/Serbia.png" alt="Serbia - Type Approval Regulatory news">
            
            
            
        </div>
            <div class="infobox-content">
                    <div class="infobox-title-section">
                <h2 class="title">Serbia</h2>            </div>
            <div><p>24-10-2024</p></div>        </div>
            </div>

						</div>
				</div>
					</div>
		</div>
				<div class="has_eae_slider elementor-column elementor-col-50 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-a820e70" data-eae-slider="17315" data-id="a820e70" data-element_type="column">
			<div class="elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated">
						<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-08504a8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="08504a8" data-element_type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h2 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Serbia Introduces New Radio Equipment Regulations: Transition to CE Marking

</h2>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-07d32f1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor" data-id="07d32f1" data-element_type="widget" data-widget_type="text-editor.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
									<p>The Regulatory Authority for Electronic Communications and Postal Services (RATEL) in Serbia has introduced a new Rulebook on Radio Equipment, published on March 22, 2024. These regulations apply to all radio equipment but exclude categories like equipment for radio amateurs and those used in marine, aviation, and state security activities.</p><p>A key change is the transition from Serbian Certificates of Conformity (CoCs) to CE Marking, recognized in the EU. Starting June 1, 2024, new CoCs will be valid for five years. After December 31, 2026, Serbian CoCs will no longer be required, and from January 1, 2027, only the CE Mark will be necessary for radio products in Serbia.</p><p>The timeline for this transition includes:<br />    &#8211; June 1, 2024: New regulations take effect.<br />    &#8211; Until December 31, 2026: Existing CoCs can still be used.<br />    &#8211; From January 1, 2027: CE Mark becomes the sole certification mark for the market.</p><p>This phased approach aims to ease the transition for manufacturers and suppliers.</p><p> </p><p> </p>								</div>
				</div>
					</div>
		</div>
					</div>
		</section>
				</div>
